---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TrustBadges from '../../components/TrustBadges.astro';

const title = "Why Your AC Is Blowing Warm Air — 5 Common Causes | D&H Tucson";
const description = "AC running but blowing warm air in Tucson? Here are the 5 most common causes and what to do about each before calling a technician.";
const canonical = "https://dandhac.com/blog/why-ac-blows-warm-air";
const publishDate = "May 1, 2025";
const readTime = "5 min read";
const category = "Troubleshooting";

const articleSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Why Your AC Is Blowing Warm Air — 5 Common Causes",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "D&H Air Conditioning & Heating & Plumbing" },
  "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "D&H Air Conditioning", "url": "https://dandhac.com" },
  "datePublished": "2025-05-01",
  "mainEntityOfPage": canonical
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schema={articleSchema}>

  <!-- ── Hero ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-[var(--color-navy)] to-[var(--color-navy-dark)] hero-pattern relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 md:py-20 relative">
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-blue-400 mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-blue-200 transition-colors">Home</a>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
        <a href="/blog" class="hover:text-blue-200 transition-colors">Blog</a>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="10" height="10" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg>
        <span class="text-blue-200">Troubleshooting</span>
      </nav>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-5">
        <span class="bg-red-500/20 text-red-300 text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full">{category}</span>
        <span class="text-blue-300 text-xs">{publishDate}</span>
        <span class="text-blue-400 text-xs">· {readTime}</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="font-display font-extrabold text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-white leading-[1.1] mb-5">
        Why Your AC Is Blowing Warm Air — 5 Common Causes
      </h1>
      <p class="text-blue-200 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        Your system is running, the fans are spinning, but the air coming out is warm. Here's what's happening — and what to do about each cause.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Article Content -->
  <article class="py-14 bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-[var(--color-charcoal)]">

        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-muted)] mb-8">
          In Tucson's summer heat, an AC blowing warm air isn't just uncomfortable — it's a real health risk. Here are the five most common causes and a quick guide to diagnosing them before you call.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">1. Wrong thermostat setting</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Before anything else: check your thermostat. Make sure it's set to <strong>Cool</strong> and not <strong>Heat</strong> or <strong>Fan Only</strong>. Also confirm the temperature is set <em>below</em> the current room temperature. It sounds obvious, but it's the cause of at least 10% of the calls we get.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">2. Refrigerant leak</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Refrigerant is the substance that actually cools the air. If your system has a leak, refrigerant levels drop and the system loses its cooling capacity. Signs of a refrigerant leak include warm air from the vents, ice forming on the refrigerant lines, and hissing or bubbling sounds near the unit. This requires a licensed technician — refrigerant handling is regulated and can't be DIY'd.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">3. Dirty air filter causing evaporator coil freeze</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          A clogged filter restricts airflow. When airflow drops too low, the evaporator coil gets too cold and freezes over — and a frozen coil can't exchange heat. The result: warm air (or no air at all) from the vents. Fix: turn off the AC, let the coil thaw for 2–3 hours with the fan running, then replace the filter. If it freezes again, there may be another issue.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">4. Tripped circuit breaker</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          Central AC systems have two circuits: one for the air handler inside and one for the condenser outside. If the outdoor condenser breaker trips, the fan continues running — blowing uncooled air. Check your breaker panel. If the outdoor condenser breaker is tripped, reset it once. If it trips again immediately, call us — there's an underlying electrical issue that needs attention.
        </p>

        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-2xl text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mt-10 mb-4">5. Failed compressor or capacitor</h2>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
          The compressor is the heart of your AC system. If it fails, the system can't refrigerate air no matter how long it runs. A faulty capacitor (the component that starts and runs the compressor and fan motors) is a more common and cheaper repair. Both require a technician to diagnose. The good news: a bad capacitor is one of the most common AC repairs and usually costs well under $300.
        </p>

        <div class="bg-[var(--color-cloud)] border border-[var(--color-border)] rounded-2xl p-6 my-10">
          <h3 class="font-display font-bold text-lg text-[var(--color-charcoal)] mb-3">When to call a technician</h3>
          <p class="text-[var(--color-muted)] text-sm leading-relaxed">
            If checking the thermostat and filter doesn't resolve the issue — or if you see ice forming on the unit, hear unusual noises, or smell a burning smell — turn off the system and call us. Running a malfunctioning AC can turn a small repair into a much larger one.
          </p>
          <a href="/air-conditioning-repair" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 mt-4 text-[var(--color-navy)] font-bold text-sm hover:text-[var(--color-orange)] transition-colors">
            Schedule AC repair →
          </a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <!-- Trust Badges -->
  <TrustBadges />

  <!-- Final CTA -->
  <section class="bg-[var(--color-navy)] py-14">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="font-display font-extrabold text-3xl text-white mb-4">Still blowing warm? We'll fix it today.</h2>
      <p class="text-blue-200 text-lg mb-8">Same-day AC repair available. NATE-certified techs. Upfront pricing.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="/contact" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 bg-[var(--color-orange)] hover:bg-[var(--color-orange-dark)] text-white font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-xl transition-colors shadow-lg">
          Schedule Repair
        </a>
        <a href="tel:5204082665" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 border-2 border-white text-white hover:bg-white hover:text-[var(--color-navy)] font-bold text-lg px-8 py-4 rounded-xl transition-colors">
          (520) 408-2665
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
